  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating Cuban low-carbon and circular solutions for micro-, small and medium-sized enterprises</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to reduce greenhouse gas emissions by promoting, supporting, and accelerating innovative decarbonization enterprises, materials, and business models across Cuba#s residential, tourism, and industrial sectors. By improving waste management, advancing low-carbon materials, and strengthening local supply chains, the project will help optimize resource use and drive the transition toward sustainable industrial practices.  To achieve this, the project will enhance regulatory frameworks, establish knowledge-sharing networks, and support industries in adopting waste-reducing and low-carbon strategies. Collaboration with government agencies, industry stakeholders, and research institutions will ensure an enabling environment for decarbonization, fostering innovation and economic resilience while contributing to Cuba#s broader environmental goals.</narrative>
  </description>
